.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_TIME_CLASS 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_time_unit ,
.Nm dtfl_time_total ,
.Nm dtfl_time_u64 ,
.Nm dtfl_time_u32 ,
.Nm dtfl_time_duration ,
.Nm dtfl_time_product ,
.Nm dtfl_time_lex ,
.Nm dtfl_time_altneu ,
.Nm dtfl_time_pointstamp ,
.Nm dtfl_time_class_retain ,
.Nm dtfl_time_class_free ,
.Nm dtfl_time_depth ,
.Nm dtfl_summary_depth ,
.Nm dtfl_time_is_total
.Nd timestamp classes
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/time.h
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_unit void
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_total "dtfl_coord coord"
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_u64 void
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_u32 void
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_duration void
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_product "const dtfl_time_class *outer" "const dtfl_time_class *inner"
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_lex "const dtfl_time_class *first" "const dtfl_time_class *second"
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_altneu "const dtfl_time_class *base"
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_pointstamp "dtfl_coord coord" "unsigned max_len"
.Ft dtfl_time_class *
.Fn dtfl_time_class_retain "const dtfl_time_class *tc"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_time_class_free "const dtfl_time_class *tc"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn dtfl_time_depth "const dtfl_time_class *tc"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn dtfl_summary_depth "const dtfl_time_class *tc"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_time_is_total "const dtfl_time_class *tc"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A timestamp in libdtfl is a vector of
.Vt uint64_t
words.
A
.Vt dtfl_time_class
gives the vector its length, its
.Em depth ,
and its meaning.
Each class models one Rust timestamp type of timely and differential
dataflow, and its operations behave as that type's do; see
.Xr dtfl_time_cmp 3
and
.Xr dtfl_summary_results_in 3 .
No time or summary is longer than
.Dv DTFL_TIME_MAX
(16) words.
.Pp
A
.Vt dtfl_coord
describes one integer coordinate:
.Bl -tag -width DTFL_COORD_UNSIGNED
.It Dv DTFL_COORD_UNSIGNED
an unsigned integer of
.Fa bits
8, 16, 32 or 64, stored as its value.
.It Dv DTFL_COORD_SIGNED
a signed integer of
.Fa bits
8, 16, 32 or 64, stored biased (see
.Xr dtfl_coord_from_i64 3 ) .
.It Dv DTFL_COORD_DURATION
a Rust
.Vt Duration
in nanoseconds;
.Fa bits
is 64.
Durations of 2^64 nanoseconds (about 584 years) or more are not
representable.
.El
.Pp
The constructors:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fn dtfl_time_unit
models
.Li () :
depth 0, and every time is equal.
.It Fn dtfl_time_total
models an integer or
.Vt Duration :
depth 1, totally ordered.
.Fn dtfl_time_u64 ,
.Fn dtfl_time_u32
and
.Fn dtfl_time_duration
are shorthands for the common coordinates.
.It Fn dtfl_time_product
models
.Vt Product<outer, inner> ,
ordered by the product order.
The outer words come first.
.It Fn dtfl_time_lex
models the tuple
.Vt (first, second) ,
ordered lexicographically.
.It Fn dtfl_time_altneu
models dogsdogsdogs'
.Vt AltNeu<T>
over a one-coordinate unsigned or Duration
.Fa base ,
stored in one word as 2t + neu.
Times t of 2^63 or more do not fit.
.It Fn dtfl_time_pointstamp
models
.Vt PointStamp<T>
over an unsigned or Duration coordinate, stored padded with zero
(the minimum) to
.Fa max_len
words.
.Fa max_len
is between 1 and
.Dv DTFL_TIME_MAX
- 1, because a summary needs
.Fa max_len
+ 1 words.
.El
.Pp
Classes are reference counted.
Each constructor returns a class with one reference, owned by the
caller.
.Fn dtfl_time_class_retain
adds a reference and returns its argument.
.Fn dtfl_time_class_free
drops one, and frees the class with the last; it accepts
.Dv NULL .
A composite class holds a reference to each child, so the caller may
free the children as soon as the composite exists.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_time_depth
returns the number of words in a time, and
.Fn dtfl_summary_depth
the number in a path summary.
.Fn dtfl_time_is_total
returns true when the partial order is total, as Rust's
.Vt TotalOrder
marker says: integers,
.Vt Duration ,
.Li () ,
.Vt AltNeu ,
tuples of total orders, and
.Vt Product
whose outer class has depth 0 and whose inner class is total.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The constructors return a new class, or
.Dv NULL
with an error detail for
.Xr dtfl_last_error_detail 3 .
They do not return
.Dv NULL
for lack of memory; allocation failure calls the panic hook.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The time of an iterative scope inside a
.Vt u64
dataflow,
.Vt Product<u64, u32> :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_time_class *outer = dtfl_time_u64();
dtfl_time_class *inner = dtfl_time_u32();
dtfl_time_class *tc = dtfl_time_product(outer, inner);

dtfl_time_class_free(outer);
dtfl_time_class_free(inner);
/* dtfl_time_depth(tc) == 2 */
dtfl_time_class_free(tc);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
A constructor returns
.Dv NULL
when:
.Bl -bullet
.It
a coordinate has an unsupported kind or width;
.It
a child of
.Fn dtfl_time_product
or
.Fn dtfl_time_lex
is
.Dv NULL ,
or the result would exceed
.Dv DTFL_TIME_MAX
words of time or of summary;
.It
the base of
.Fn dtfl_time_altneu
is not a one-coordinate unsigned or Duration class;
.It
.Fn dtfl_time_pointstamp
gets a signed coordinate, or
.Fa max_len
outside 1 to
.Dv DTFL_TIME_MAX
- 1.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_summary_results_in 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_time_cmp 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
Rust timely dataflow is generic over the
.Vt Timestamp
trait (timely/src/progress/timestamp.rs at timely-v0.31.0).
A C library cannot be, so a class carries at run time what the Rust
type carries at compile time.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
Classes are immutable after construction, and their reference count
is atomic, so a class may be shared, retained and freed from any
thread.
